egressions ```"],["db6a4611_2f969de3",21,0,0,"(Non for this CL) Is this code strongly owned by any team? If so can you add OWNERS files at https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:chrome/browser/ui/webui/device_log/. Also the…"]],0,768],[7262376,20437,4,0.248,0.178,[[32,28]],[],0,769],[7266987,20439,759,10.952,8.912,[[32,0.923,29,893],[4,0.068,49,61],[13,0.007,136,6],[71,0.002,0,1]],[["0898e8b2_704db4f1",26,0,1,"Add a TODO here about adding real tests? This assertion is otherwise somewhat useless, as createElement() can never fail, regardless of whether device-log-app is the element you think it is."],["64a3dd08_85d51725",27,0,0,"Is the <span> needed? ```suggestion <div id=\"header\">$i18n{autoRefreshText}</div> ```"],["97ad82f1_3c9d523f",28,0,1,"All of these can be deleted now that SetupWebUIDataSource() is called."],["ded45776_400d7fbd",29,0,1,"Nit: This usuaully appears at the end of the file."],["ecdd2c6c_6829af3f",29,0,0,"All of these listeners can be more simply added using Lit expressions now. For example ``` <button id=\"logFileinfo\" @click=\"${this.onLogFileInfoClick}\">...</button> ``` And more generally there are a…"],["ef126037_2d9fbc82",30,0,1,"Move this to <body>."]],0,770],[7270030,20441,439,7.579,6.176,[[32,0.95,30,415],[72,0.05,0,20]],[["014d5400_87777a65",29,-1,1,"Why were this made public? Please see `changedPrivateProperties` if using this in willUpdate was the only reason you made them public. [1]…"],["2352ac63_0f06002b",27,-1,1,"Fits in one line."],["3b3f79d8_a5efba50",27,-1,1,"This is an anti-pattern. See https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/webui/webui_lit_style_guide.md#logic_free-templates. Can you make `filteredLogs_` a computed property instead…"],["3ec2a4d5_3857de8b",29,-1,1,"FWIW, per our current conventions, it is OK to omit `void` as a return type (here and elsewhere). My previous comment implied adding return types anywhere where something other than `void` is…"],["48b397d1_6118a14c",29,-1,1,"Unnecessary annotation? TS can already infer this."],["569e4099_6b31740d",29,-1,1,"Can just combine this by passing an array to the Set's constructor, and use Array#filter instead. ```suggestion const enabledEvents: Set<string> = new Set( this.eventTypes_.filter(type =>…"],["68cd0282_3a83b415",29,-1,1,"Please remove this suppression and update the names below. The name can be capital without affecting the value. ```suggestion /* eslint-disable @typescript-eslint/naming-convention */ // LogLevel…"],["8fca8560_a3c8bcf3",29,-1,1,"Should this be turned into an `enum` ? Then you can use the enum in the html.ts file as well and avoid repeating the same string literals."],["97b478a7_92f49ea4",29,-1,1,"Need to call `super.willUpdate(...)` here."],["ac21386c_f5fc3a54",27,-1,1,"Move this part to the previous line?"],["bfa86eea_f8348168",29,-1,1,"Declare return types explicitly. (here and elsewhere)"],["ca134599_1bd636c4",27,-1,1,"Enum values should be capital letters. ```suggestion <option value=\"${LogLevel.ERROR}\">$i18n{logLevelErrorText}</option> ``` (here and elsewhere) Are you sure this is not caught by our presubmit…"],["d10b1217_4bb275c4",27,-1,1,"Typo?"],["e4995745_06d6c8d6",27,-1,1,"Optinoal: Wrap text contents with a span? It is a bit odd to have a text node be a sibling with a `<p>` ```suggestion ${logs.length === 0 ? html`<span>$i18n{logNoEntriesText}</span>` : ``} ```"],["ea955b41_d9685a53",27,-1,1,"Can you rename all these handlers to follow oru naming conventions ? See [1] For example this one should be named as follows ```suggestion <button id=\"logRefresh\" @click=\"${this.onLogRefreshClick_}\">…"],["f6cdd914_f7868bf5",27,-1,1,"Is this container div needed? All of a custom element's HTML is already contained by the shadow DOM's root node. Let's remove?"],["f8b076e4_0cd6a5c7",29,-1,1,"Wrap arrow function body with curly braces if it takes up multiple lines. The shorthand syntax should only be used when it is actually short. (here and elsewhere)"],["fc6196ce_2f8c7e32",27,-1,1,"Rename this to `item`. Also see our styleguide at https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/webui/webui_lit_style_guide.md#loop-variables (here and elsewhere in this file)"],["feadf8a4_c2608c52",27,-1,1,"Fits in one line."],["175fa134_36bd84f2",29,0,1,"```suggestion checkedTypesInput.includes(type.toLowerCase()), ```"],["83f0f739_3de85cf9",29,0,1,"```suggestion const target = event.target as HTMLSelectElement; ```"],["8d2b881c_ee12591d",29,0,1,"Optional: Perhaps refer to the exact C++ enum's location if it exists?"],["a1c7e332_472822f4",29,0,1,"I don't quite understand the conversion being done here. Shouldn't this simply be as follows? ``` this.selectedLogLevel_ = taget.value as LogLevel; ```"],["c243a783_afbcdeb5",29,0,1,"Nit: Move `connectedCallack()` right after the constructor. This is a more intuitive location in the code as `connectedCallback()` is related to initialization of the element."]],0,771],[7281872,20445,395,6.521,5.246,[[4,0.736,50,294],[32,0.256,31,99],[72,0.007,1,2]],[["39709bfe_e0416fd1",29,-4,1,"Please split \"import type\" and plain \"import\" to separate lines."],["43a15918_904e0c7e",26,-4,1,"Unnecessary `async`/`await`, just use `return`. ```suggestion setupfunction() { browserProxy = new TestBrowserProxy(); BrowserProxyImpl.setInstance(browserProxy); browserProxy.setLogs(testLogs);…"],["5c0ea7f9_c413e2a2",26,-4,1,"Same here. Split to separate lines."],["73d8482a_1953711b",26,-4,1,"Do this before any other line in this function."],["7cf0e6cd_b6c1f5dd",26,-4,1,"Prefer for...of instead of forEach ```suggestion const checkboxes = app.shadowRoot.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>( '#logCheckboxContainer input[type=\"checkbox\"]'); for (const checkbox of…"],["96cc5045_9b1b42d3",26,-4,1,"Why does it need to be reset?"],["98857913_0caf275d",26,-4,1,"```suggestion function getLogEntries() { return app.shadowRoot.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('#logContainer p'); } ```"],["c11ec87d_7fd1c4b3",26,-4,0,"```suggestion checkboxes.forEach(checkbox => assertFalse(checkbox.checked)); ```"],["d91dc59c_745b2e3c",26,-4,1,"Please use `microtasksFinished()` in tests (here and elsewhere instead of updateComplete)."],["14ffdca9_59273357",26,-1,1,"There shouldn't be any business logic in the test proxy and it shouldn't try to emulate what the real proxy does. The test should be responsible for calling `setLogs()` as needed."],["73838202_819170d2",26,-1,1,"Without calling `resetResolver('getLog')` after the previous call, this does not resolve when you think it does. It would resolve even if the 2nd call never happened."],["92b72767_027282ca",31,-1,1,"There shouldn't be any logic in a browser proxy, beyond calling the backend and forwarding any return values. Can you move this functionality outside of the proxy?"]],0,772],[7277547,20445,40,1.326,1.047,[[13,0.81,137,33],[35,0.095,44,3],[38,0.048,26,1],[32,0.048,32,1]],[["a7ea0ad7_3f02ba39",21,-4,1,"```suggestion Fix chrome://device-log missing the \"Memory\" log type. This seems to have been an oversight during the initial implementation of \"Memory\". ```"]],0,773],[7302412,20445,75,2.344,1.853,[[32,33]],[["50c906a5_48ad78e8",32,-1,1,"Per styleguide, should use 3-letter hex notation where possible, https://google.github.io/styleguide/htmlcssguide.html#Hexadecimal_Notation (basically wherever a shade of gray is used)"],["b5fb0210_0a3c565e",32,-1,1,"Here and elsewhere, each selector should be on its own line per styleguide. ```suggestion button, select, input { ```"]],0,774]]}